  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord of a rental unit shall pay interest to the tenant annually on the amount of the rent deposit at a rate equal to the guideline determined under section 120 that is in effect at the time payment becomes due.",
  "reason": "The clause requires the landlord to pay annual interest on the rent deposit at the rate of the rent increase guideline in effect when the payment is due. This directly matches the statutory requirement set out in section 106(6) of the Act, so it is consistent with the Act and permitted."
}

